ithub.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot v4.6.2 on MacOS\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.2.stable - macOS Tahoe (26.0.1) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Mobile) - integrated Apple M2 (Apple8) - Apple M2 (8 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nShift + Scroll scrolls **vertically** in 2D editor rather than **horizontally** on MacOS after setting `2D editor panning scheme` to `Scroll Pans`\n\nI tried searching online to see if I made any mistakes on y side or if this feature doesn't work on mac but I didn't find anyone mentioning it. I found that this feature is already implemented in this [PR](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/39687) and it works on windows but not on MacOS.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open a new project in Godot v4.6.2 on MacOS\n2. In `Settings`->Editors`->`Panning` , set `2D editor panning scheme` to `Scroll Pans`.\n3. In 2D editor, press Shift and try scrolling with a mouse wheel. Instead of scrolling horizontally it's gonna scroll vertically.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThe issue is reproducible in a  new project ","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118981/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118981/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinn